"about": "Invented projects and thoughts for placing among many (docs/projects-design.md, Experiments). The first 36 and the first 100 projects are the smaller sets; every thought's target is among the first 36, six of which are named with everyday words (app, test, notes, docs, site, scripts). quiet: days since something happened there. kind of a thought: named, spoken (as a recogniser writes the name), twin (the name has near-duplicates), described, described-blind (the target's card says nothing), none (no project is meant: it must not be placed). seen: the review's examples, which the rules were changed for (in-sample). decoy: no project is meant, though a word of it is an everyday-word project's name, sounds like one or is two words of one; written after the rules and not used to change them (held out); placed is wrong, asked or kept is right. everyday: an everyday-word project used as a name (held out).",
